From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sensor: only replace a matrix when all entries are zero

An integer sum truncates floating-point values and cannot distinguish an
all-zero matrix from a nonzero rotation whose entries cancel. Preserve
every supplied nonzero entry; keep the existing warning for actual zeros.

The same predicate is present in upstream main at
4e4c6c8cc702a754bd700506c01961aaf971a23b. No device matrix or
calibration value is added.

Signed-off-by: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/src/libssc-sensor.c b/src/libssc-sensor.c
--- a/src/libssc-sensor.c
+++ b/src/libssc-sensor.c
@@ -407,15 +407,16 @@
 					}
 
 					/* Fallback to identity matrix in case matrix is all 0 */
-					gint sum = 0;
+					gboolean all_zero = TRUE;
 					for (gsize k = 0; k < 9; k++)
-						sum += priv->mount_matrix[k/3][k%3];
+						all_zero &= priv->mount_matrix[k/3][k%3] == 0.0f;
 
-					if (sum == 0) {
+					if (all_zero) {
 						priv->mount_matrix[0][0] = 1.0;
 						priv->mount_matrix[1][1] = 1.0;
 						priv->mount_matrix[2][2] = 1.0;
-						g_warning ("Mount matrix provided by firmware is all 0, falling back to identity matrix!");
+						g_warning ("Mount matrix for %s is all 0, falling back to identity matrix!",
+							   priv->data_type ? priv->data_type : "unknown");
 					}
 					break;
 		       }
